    "security-fixes": {
      "name": "security-fixes",
      "description": "Bind web server to localhost instead of 0.0.0.0 and validate checkpoint file paths to prevent path traversal",
      "issue_ids": [
        "review::.::holistic::authorization_consistency::unsanitized_checkpoint_path",
        "review::.::holistic::authorization_consistency::web_server_binds_all_interfaces"
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-03-18T18:48:28+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-03-18T19:03:35+00:00",
      "auto": false,
      "cluster_key": "",
      "action": null,
      "action_type": "manual_fix",
      "execution_policy": "planned_only",
      "execution_status": "active",
      "user_modified": true,
      "action_steps": [
        {
          "title": "Fix web server binding and checkpoint path validation",
          "detail": "CORRECTED: This step claims checkpoint path comes only from CLI args. This is partially wrong. The initial load in run_server (server.rs:63-67) does use CLI args. However, the WebSocket handler for LoadCheckpoint (server.rs:287-291) takes path directly from user input. The bind address fix is correct: change 0.0.0.0 to 127.0.0.1 on server.rs line 104. The checkpoint path validation should be done in the LoadCheckpoint handler, adding canonicalize() and a parent-directory allowlist check before passing to sim.load_checkpoint.",
          "effort": "small",
          "issue_refs": []
        },
        {
          "title": "Change bind address in server.rs",
          "detail": "In src/web/server.rs line 104, change the format string from '0.0.0.0:{}' to '127.0.0.1:{}'. This is a single-character change in one line. The server currently binds to all interfaces which is unnecessary since this is a development/local tool.",
          "effort": "trivial",
          "issue_refs": []
        },
        {
          "title": "Add checkpoint path validation",
          "detail": "CORRECTED: The enrich report claimed unsanitized_checkpoint_path is a false positive because path comes from CLI. This is WRONG. While the initial load (server.rs:63-67) uses CLI args, the LoadCheckpoint WebSocket handler (server.rs:287-291) takes path directly from client WebSocket input and passes it to Checkpoint::load via sim.load_checkpoint. This IS a real path traversal risk. Add canonicalize() + parent-directory check before passing to Checkpoint::load in the handle_command LoadCheckpoint branch.",
          "effort": "small",
          "issue_refs": []
        },
        {
          "title": "Add tests for path validation",
          "detail": "Add a test in src/web/simulation.rs (or a new tests/web_security.rs) that calls load_checkpoint with a path containing '..' components and verifies it returns an error. Also test that a valid .json path succeeds. This requires the web feature flag to be enabled for compilation.",
          "effort": "small",
          "issue_refs": []
        }
      ]
    },
