      "auto": false,
      "cluster_key": "",
      "action": null,
      "action_type": "manual_fix",
      "execution_policy": "planned_only",
      "execution_status": "active",
      "user_modified": true,
      "action_steps": [
        {
          "title": "Add smoke tests for CLI commands",
          "detail": "Create tests/cli_smoke.rs with integration tests for CLI commands. Test that 'gilgamesh train --config configs/simple.json --epochs 1' runs without panic (use assert_cmd crate or std::process::Command). Test 'gilgamesh evaluate --checkpoint models/model.json' runs. Verify src/cli/mod.rs Cli::parse() handles known subcommands. Requires test fixtures: configs/simple.json and models/model.json already exist in the repo.",
          "effort": "medium",
          "issue_refs": []
        },
        {
          "title": "Add web layer tests",
          "detail": "Create tests/web_test.rs (gated behind #[cfg(feature = \"web\")]). Use axum::test to create a test client against the Router built in src/web/server.rs. Test GET /api/status returns 200 with valid JSON. Test WebSocket connection to /ws receives initial Status message. Requires adding axum-test or tower::ServiceExt as dev-dependency in Cargo.toml. The server setup is in src/web/server.rs run_server() function starting at line 54.",
          "effort": "medium",
          "issue_refs": []
        },
        {
          "title": "Add integration test for training pipeline",
          "detail": "Create tests/training_integration.rs. Test 1: construct a Network::new(36, 12, 10, 0.9, 42), create a Trainer, call train_epoch with a small synthetic dataset (random 36-dim inputs, random labels 0-9), verify it returns finite loss and non-zero accuracy. Test 2: verify Network::forward() with 25 timesteps produces spike counts of shape [batch, 10] with all values >= 0. Test 3: verify backward pass produces non-zero gradients. Uses src/network/network.rs, src/training.rs. No MNIST data needed - create synthetic data inline.",
          "effort": "medium",
          "issue_refs": []
        }
      ],
      "depends_on_clusters": [
        "forward-consolidation"
      ]
    }
